  "rationale": "The fleet facts show iterative is the sole contributor to the merged Pareto front (19/19 designs, best luts_plus_ffs 300), while unrolled_k (best 730), pipelined (1548) and pipelined_m (838) all sit far off the front and contribute nothing. Since I am restricted to iterative and unrolled_k, and unrolled_k has already been shown to be strictly dominated in area (730 vs 300) with 0 front members, the entire remaining budget should go to iterative. The first 73 evals covered the full registry ranges; now that the feasible region is known (data_width ~12-16, n_iter ~10-16, small guards), I narrow the ranges to focus the search on the actual trade-off curve between luts_plus_ffs and accuracy_bits. This maximizes hypervolume by densely covering the feasible Pareto segment rather than wasting evals on infeasible or dominated configurations. unrolled_k is excluded because its best area (730) is 2.4x worse than iterative's best (300) and it has contributed zero designs to the front, so it cannot improve hypervolume within the remaining budget."
